1
00:00:10,199 --> 00:00:13,920
Now I'm in my spaceship.
Now I'm on my way.

2
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,004
I'm going to a party.

3
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,970
Hip! Hip! Hip! Hooray!

4
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:22,165
Hi. I'm Muzzy.

5
00:00:22,399 --> 00:00:24,128
Big Muzzy.

6
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:45,644
A hundred and fifty trees
there...

7
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:50,483
and thirty trees here.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,683
Oh, hello. I'm Bob.

9
00:00:59,119 --> 00:01:01,360
Hello. I'm Norman.

10
00:01:02,359 --> 00:01:04,487
Welcome to Gondoland!

11
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:07,323
That's the Palace.

12
00:01:08,239 --> 00:01:09,729
And there's the King.

13
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:13,481
How do you do?
I'm the King of Gondoland.

14
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:17,686
And there's the Queen.

15
00:01:18,079 --> 00:01:21,241
How do you do?
I'm the Queen.

16
00:01:21,439 --> 00:01:24,648
And their daughter,
Princess Sylvia.

17
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,242
Hello!

18
00:01:27,319 --> 00:01:29,400
And Sylvia's husband, Bob.

19
00:01:34,959 --> 00:01:36,483
Hey, Bob!

20
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,284
-Are you there?
-Who's that?

21
00:01:38,519 --> 00:01:40,680
It's me! Muzzy!

22
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:46,003
Ah! Hello, Muzzy.
How are you?

23
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,725
I'm fine, thanks.

24
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,843
What time is the party?

25
00:01:51,239 --> 00:01:54,049
It's at half past five this
afternoon.

26
00:01:54,439 --> 00:01:57,089
Oh dear!
Am I late?

27
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:00,802
No, you aren't late, Muzzy.
You're early.

28
00:02:01,159 --> 00:02:03,605
-Early?
-Yes.

29
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:05,927
The party's at half past five.

30
00:02:08,039 --> 00:02:10,406
What time is it now?

31
00:02:12,199 --> 00:02:13,963
What time is it?

32
00:02:14,319 --> 00:02:16,640
It's eight o'clock.

33
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:21,401
See you at ten o'clock.

34
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,251
Bye!

35
00:02:24,199 --> 00:02:25,963
Don't be late!

36
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,804
Where is he?

37
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:37,523
Ten fifteen.

38
00:02:37,759 --> 00:02:39,840
Quarter past ten.

39
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:42,048
Ten thirty.

40
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:44,328
Half past ten.

41
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,801
Ten forty-five.

42
00:02:47,039 --> 00:02:48,722
Quarter to eleven.

43
00:02:49,719 --> 00:02:52,040
He's late again.

44
00:02:54,919 --> 00:02:56,602
You're late.

45
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,881
No, I'm not. I'm early.

46
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:00,964
It's quarter to ten.

47
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,801
It isn't. It's...

48
00:03:06,199 --> 00:03:08,327
eleven o'clock.

49
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,968
Oh dear! I am late.

50
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,488
But I've got this for you !

51
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,845
What's the time in Gondoland?

52
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:26,006
It's ten fifteen.
quarter past ten in the morning.

53
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,401
Oh!

54
00:03:27,639 --> 00:03:30,289
This clock here says
quarter to three.

55
00:03:30,759 --> 00:03:33,807
And this one says
half past four...

56
00:03:36,639 --> 00:03:37,685
Ah!

57
00:03:37,879 --> 00:03:40,200
This one says ten fifteen.

58
00:03:40,599 --> 00:03:42,203
Quarter past ten.

59
00:03:42,439 --> 00:03:44,247
So you're early.

60
00:03:44,759 --> 00:03:46,204
Where's Sylvia?

61
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:49,050
I don't know...

62
00:03:49,879 --> 00:03:52,165
but we've got a surprise for you.

63
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,930
A surprise!

64
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:57,329
-What is it?
-Aha! It's a secret.

65
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,925
Tell me.

66
00:03:59,159 --> 00:04:01,969
No. It's a secret.

67
00:04:02,199 --> 00:04:03,963
Wait and see.

68
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:07,091
Oh, all right.

69
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:09,488
See you at the party!

70
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,966
See you!

71
00:04:13,319 --> 00:04:16,084
Ah! There you are!

72
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,644
It's not a secret.

73
00:04:21,839 --> 00:04:23,762
It's Amanda.

74
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,480
And whose baby are you?

75
00:04:26,879 --> 00:04:30,041
-She's ours, of course.
-Yes.

76
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,810
You're our baby.

77
00:04:32,079 --> 00:04:34,320
And whose fingers are these?

78
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:37,090
They're Amanda's fingers.

79
00:04:37,279 --> 00:04:41,408
And whose toes are these?

80
00:04:41,879 --> 00:04:44,165
They're Amanda's toes.

81
00:04:44,519 --> 00:04:46,442
They're hers.

82
00:04:46,639 --> 00:04:50,121
And whose eyes are these?

83
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,171
They're your eyes, Amanda.

84
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,840
Yes, they're yours.

85
00:04:56,279 --> 00:04:59,521
And this is your little nose.

86
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,485
Yours!

87
00:05:07,639 --> 00:05:10,289
How many fingers?

88
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:12,686
How many toes?

89
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:15,081
How many eyes

90
00:05:15,279 --> 00:05:17,520
Beside her nose?

91
00:05:22,839 --> 00:05:25,729
Ten little fingers.

92
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,809
Ten little toes.

93
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,843
Two big brown eyes.

94
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:32,486
And a little pink nose.

95
00:05:32,759 --> 00:05:37,640
Two big brown eyes.
And a little pink nose.

96
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:43,882
And how many teeth? Ow!

97
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:46,208
Naughty Amanda!

98
00:05:46,519 --> 00:05:48,487
Come on, off we go!

99
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:51,928
Are we ready for the party?

100
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,691
Nearly. We're nearly ready.

101
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,367
Corvax is making a cake.

102
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,483
A huge cake!

103
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,444
An enormous cake!

104
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:16,569
Now what does it say here?

105
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:20,124
Er... what do we need?

106
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,725
Flour. I need flour...

107
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,763
Sugar... Currants...

108
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,924
Oh, I hate this job.

109
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:37,402
How do you do?
I'm Corvax.

110
00:06:38,199 --> 00:06:41,282
Eggs, butter...

111
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:48,247
Oh dear! I need help.

112
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,847
Here you are, Corvax!

113
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,883
He can help you.

114
00:07:01,519 --> 00:07:05,001
Be good,
or you go back to prison.

115
00:07:07,839 --> 00:07:09,568
Who are you?

116
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,763
What's your name?

117
00:07:14,199 --> 00:07:15,689
I'm Thimbo.

118
00:07:15,959 --> 00:07:17,529
Thimbo the terrible!

119
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,324
I'm bad!

120
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:22,609
Bad are you? Aha!

121
00:07:23,079 --> 00:07:25,127
I know you. You're Corvax.

122
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:28,045
-You're very bad.
-Yes.

123
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,124
And I'm clever.

124
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:32,927
What are you doing, Corvax?

125
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,885
I'm making a cake.
A huge cake.

126
00:07:36,079 --> 00:07:38,525
An enormous cake.

127
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,041
Now get some sugar
and some eggs

128
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:43,446
and some apples and...

129
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,603
I hate work!

130
00:07:49,879 --> 00:07:51,562
I hate work.

131
00:07:51,759 --> 00:07:56,446
And I hate Bob
and I hate Muzzy.

132
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:59,840
Muzzy? Who's Muzzy?

133
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,530
Wait and see!

134
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:04,925
The party's for Muzzy.

135
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,446
What food does he like?

136
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:11,003
-Clocks.
-Clocks!

137
00:08:11,399 --> 00:08:13,605
Does he eat clocks?

138
00:08:13,879 --> 00:08:16,120
Yes, he does.

139
00:08:16,519 --> 00:08:18,647
Muzzy eats clocks.

140
00:08:18,839 --> 00:08:21,524
Now, you get on with your work!

141
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:26,962
I hate Muzzy
and I hate Bob.

142
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,527
But I love Princess Sylvia.

143
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:50,883
Hello, Muzzy.

144
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:53,128
Welcome to Gondoland!

145
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,650
Hello, Bob...

146
00:08:54,879 --> 00:08:56,722
Your Majesty!

147
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:59,321
Glad to see you again, Muzzy.

148
00:08:59,519 --> 00:09:01,408
Oh, Muzzy!

149
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:04,080
It is nice to see you.

150
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,687
It's a pleasure, your Majesty!

151
00:09:07,399 --> 00:09:10,528
-And here's our secret.
-Sylvia!

152
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:14,087
A baby!
What a nice surprise!

153
00:09:14,279 --> 00:09:18,408
-Is it your baby?
-Yes, it's ours.

154
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,249
Of course it's theirs.

155
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:24,047
And what's its... his... her...

156
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:27,682
She's a girl.
Her name's Amanda.

157
00:09:27,879 --> 00:09:31,246
Hello, Amanda. Ow!

158
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:34,526
Does she often bite people?

159
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:38,041
-Sometimes.
-Oh, Bob!

160
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:41,642
Not often.
She doesn't often bite people.

161
00:09:41,879 --> 00:09:43,927
She always bites me.

162
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:46,043
Now she's biting me!

163
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:49,802
I'm wearing trousers.

164
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:52,288
I always wear trousers.

165
00:09:53,279 --> 00:09:55,327
I'm wearing a skin.

166
00:09:55,519 --> 00:09:57,805
I usually wear a skin,

167
00:09:59,159 --> 00:10:01,605
but I sometimes wear trousers.

168
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,570
Yes, you do.

169
00:10:03,759 --> 00:10:06,205
And I never wear a skin.

170
00:10:09,159 --> 00:10:11,002
He wears trousers.

171
00:10:11,559 --> 00:10:13,926
But he often takes them off.

172
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,648
And the dog always
brings them back.

173
00:10:21,639 --> 00:10:24,289
Now, what do we need?

174
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:26,288
Do we need any salt?

175
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:28,601
Ah! Yes, we do.

176
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:31,727
Is there any salt over there?

177
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:35,168
Yes, there is.

178
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:37,448
There's some in here.

179
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:44,244
Ahchoo!

180
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:49,081
Do we need any pepper?

181
00:10:49,279 --> 00:10:51,327
No, we don't.

182
00:10:51,519 --> 00:10:53,919
We don't need any pepper.

183
00:11:03,159 --> 00:11:04,729
I want some rice.

184
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,201
Have you got any rice?

185
00:11:08,639 --> 00:11:12,200
I haven't got any rice, but...

186
00:11:12,639 --> 00:11:15,039
I've got some cheese.

187
00:11:16,559 --> 00:11:18,640
Do you want any cheese?

188
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,604
No, thank you.

189
00:11:21,799 --> 00:11:23,927
I don't want any cheese.

190
00:11:25,399 --> 00:11:27,527
I want some apples.

191
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:29,961
Have you got any apples?

192
00:11:31,159 --> 00:11:33,160
I haven't got any apples,

193
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:37,047
but I've got some biscuits.

194
00:11:39,639 --> 00:11:42,324
I don't want any biscuits.

195
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,281
Have you got any eggs?

196
00:11:47,799 --> 00:11:51,166
Ah! Some eggs.

197
00:11:53,759 --> 00:11:57,161
No I haven't got any eggs.

198
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:59,328
How about some flowers?

199
00:11:59,919 --> 00:12:04,446
No, thank you.
I don't want any flowers.

200
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,690
Good morning!!

201
00:12:07,519 --> 00:12:09,168
What about milk?

202
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:11,368
Do we need any milk?

203
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,850
Look at the book!
Read it!

204
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:19,249
I don't know!

205
00:12:20,399 --> 00:12:22,924
Oh! You can't read.

206
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:25,323
No, I can't.

207
00:12:26,679 --> 00:12:29,284
Well, then, get some plates.

208
00:12:32,799 --> 00:12:34,960
I can't see any plates.

209
00:12:35,519 --> 00:12:38,362
There are some plates over there.

210
00:12:39,399 --> 00:12:42,049
No, there aren't.
There aren't any.

211
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,885
Yes, there are. Look!

212
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,803
In front of you.

213
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,847
Oh! Those plates!

214
00:12:54,679 --> 00:12:56,840
Be careful!

215
00:13:08,519 --> 00:13:11,966
What's happening?
What's all this?

216
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,685
Who are you?

217
00:13:13,879 --> 00:13:16,120
I'm Thimbo.

218
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:18,891
-Where's Corvax?
-Over there!

219
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,320
Where?

220
00:13:20,559 --> 00:13:22,323
He's there, your Majesty.

221
00:13:22,559 --> 00:13:25,721
Don't be stupid!
Corvax isn't here.

222
00:13:25,919 --> 00:13:27,842
Get on with your work!

223
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,887
Corvax!

224
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:33,487
-Where are you?
-I'm here.

225
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:38,885
Wow! That's clever!

226
00:13:39,159 --> 00:13:40,445
Can I do that?

227
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:43,001
No, you can't.
It's a secret.

228
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:46,283
But perhaps...

229
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:50,921
Ah, yes! Yes!

230
00:13:51,159 --> 00:13:53,048
I've got a surprise.

231
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:57,244
A surprise for the King...
and for Bob.

232
00:13:57,799 --> 00:14:00,085
And for everyone.

233
00:14:01,399 --> 00:14:03,242
And you can help me.

